WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
In 1950, Timothy Evans
was hanged for murder.

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.420
In 1966, he received a pardon.

3
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.210
Britain's last executions came in 1964.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.710
Yet the debate over the death
penalty has never gone away.

5
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.530
In 2018, the Catholic Church's
Catechism called it inadmissible.

6
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.100
So should punishment pay back
the past or protect the future?

7
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.790
And may a state ever take a life?

8
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.530
In this mission, you'll sort 5 purposes
of punishment along that arrow.

9
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.920
Then you'll weigh the case for
and against the death penalty,

10
00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.610
theory by theory.

11
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.790
Your mission: weigh up
what punishment is for,

12
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.270
and whether a state may ever take a life.
